% against F. Chung's publication list (authors, title, journal, volume, pages, year; the DOI was not verified then
% and was left out).
% Exact source for the diameter of G(n,p) as recorded 2026-10-07: (1+o(1)) log n / log(np) if np tends
% to infinity; for np/log n = c > c0 the diameter is concentrated on finitely many values.
% Corrected 2026-10-09 after reading the authors' PDF (fanchung.ucsd.edu/dia.pdf, Section 4, p. 15):
% (1+o(1)) log n / log(np) is Theorem 5 and needs log n > np -> infinity (below the connectivity threshold).
% For p >= c log n / n with a constant c, Theorem 4 gives almost surely
% ceil(log(cn/11)/log(np)) <= diam <= ceil(log(33 c^2 n log n / 400)/log(np)) + 2 floor(1/c) + 2.
% The journal numbering was not compared (ScienceDirect refused the request). Note: knowledge/literature/ChungLu2001.md.
% Recommended for Theorem VI.2 of article 1 (so far only Bollobas2001 is cited there).
@article{ChungLu2001,
